    </table>
  </div>
</details>
<% end %>

<h2 id="maintenance">Maintaining complete coverage</h2>

After a Home Assistant upgrade, compare the source registries before you change any count. Add or retire an entry only with its exact source evidence, its design owner and a meaningful example. Keep explicit aliases while the native source supports them. Review changes to capabilities and meaning even when the key is the same. A renamed file is not automatically a new public feature.

The JSON records source paths, pinned commits, hashes, index members, extraction methods, expected identifiers and mappings. It stays reference-only, and a successful documentation build does not change that. Keep browser and live-device evidence separately, with the version, scenario, outcome and any limit. Review owner: Civica maintainers.
